data.content:
### What changed

- Constructor accepts an **optional** `TimeProvider` — existing callers (`new InvoiceCalculator()`) keep working with no changes.
- `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow` → `_timeProvider.GetUtcNow()`.

### In your tests

```csharp
// Add NuGet: Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing
var fake = new FakeTimeProvider(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 1, 15, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var calc = new InvoiceCalculator(fake);

Assert.True(calc.IsOverdue(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 1, 10, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero)));
fake.Advance(TimeSpan.FromDays(-30)); // move time backward
Assert.False(calc.IsOverdue(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 1, 10, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero)));
```

No DI container, no custom interfaces — just the built-in `TimeProvider` abstract class (.NET 8+) and a one-line test NuGet package.
